Read Pump.fun data through HTTP, WebSocket, and Solana RPC.
Use a read command or start the MCP server.

Use:
  pumpfun [flags]

Commands:
  coin        Read one coin.
  coins       Read coin lists.
  config      Read or change settings.
  creator     Read coin creator data.
  curve       Read bonding curve state.
  holders     Read the largest token accounts.
  mcp         Run the MCP server.
  progress    Read graduation progress.
  search      Find coins.
  stream      Read live events.
  trades      Read coin trades.
  user        Read a public user profile.

Examples:
  pumpfun coins new --output json
  pumpfun config set timeout 30s
  pumpfun mcp serve

Flags:
      --api-base-url string   Use this frontend API URL. (default "https://frontend-api-v3.pump.fun")
      --config string         Use this config file.
  -h, --help                  Show help for this command.
      --log-level string      Set the log level: trace, debug, info, warn, error, or disabled. (default "warn")
  -o, --output string         Set the output format: table, json, or yaml. (default "table")
      --rpc-url string        Use this Solana RPC URL. (default "https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com")
      --timeout string        Limit each read to this duration, such as 20s. (default "20s")
      --version               Show the program version.
      --ws-url string         Use this PumpPortal WebSocket URL. (default "wss://pumpportal.fun/api/data")
